$DIR/test.p:7:18: enum member B has the same value 0 as A
    Two members of an enum have the same value. Each value must belong to one
    member, so that converting a number to the enum, and printing a value's
    name, give one answer.
    A member without a value is one more than the member before it, which is
    often how two members end up equal.
    (see "Enums" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.12)
    (run "pluto explain E2306" for a longer explanation)
